19:T56f,## A stand-in you can't tell apart

A **Proxy** implements the **same interface** as the real object (the *subject*), so clients use it exactly as they'd use the real thing. The difference is what happens inside: the proxy holds a reference to the real subject and **decides whether, when, and how** to forward each call.

```
Image img = new ImageProxy("photo.png");
img.display();   // proxy loads the 5 MB bitmap NOW, then forwards
img.display();   // already loaded, proxy just forwards
```

Because it's a drop-in for the interface, you can slip a proxy in front of an object **without changing any calling code**.

## Four common flavours

- **Virtual**, lazy-create an expensive object on first use (don't load the 5 MB bitmap until something actually displays it).
- **Protection**, run auth / permission checks before forwarding; reject callers who aren't allowed.
- **Remote**, a local stand-in for an object that lives on another machine; the proxy handles the network round-trip.
- **Caching**, remember results and serve repeats from the cache instead of redoing the work.

## Proxy vs Decorator

Both **wrap an object of the same interface**, structurally they look alike. The **intent differs**: a Decorator *adds behaviour* to an object you already have, while a Proxy *controls access* to an object (often deciding whether the real object should exist or be reached at all).c:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex min-h-screen","children":[["$","$L17",null,{"activeModule":"lld-structural","activeLesson":"proxy"}],["$","$L18","proxy",{"lesson":{"id":"proxy","patternId":"lld-structural","title":"Proxy","kind":"pattern","difficulty":"Core","statement":"A stand-in that implements the same interface as a real object and CONTROLS access to it, to defer expensive work, check permissions, cache, or reach a remote object.","companies":["Amazon","Google","Cloudflare"],"theory":"$19","approaches":[{"label":"Same interface, a stand-in","code":["interface Image { void display(); }","class RealImage implements Image {","    RealImage(String f){ /* load 5 MB bitmap */ }","    public void display(){ /* paint pixels */ }","}","class ImageProxy implements Image {","    private RealImage real;               // the controlled subject","    public void display(){ real.display(); }","}"],"steps":[{"view":"class","codeLine":2,"narration":"Image is the interface clients depend on. RealImage is heavy, it loads a 5 MB bitmap up front, the moment it exists.","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"subj","name":"Image","stereotype":"interface","methods":["+ display()"],"x":1,"y":0.2,"tint":"accent"},{"id":"real","name":"RealImage","fields":["- 5 MB bitmap"],"methods":["+ display()"],"x":0,"y":1.6,"tint":"red"},{"id":"proxy","name":"ImageProxy","fields":["- real: RealImage"],"methods":["+ display()"],"x":1.6,"y":1.6,"tint":"accent2"}],"relations":[{"id":"r1","from":"real","to":"subj","kind":"implement"},{"id":"r2","from":"proxy","to":"subj","kind":"implement"},{"id":"r3","from":"proxy","to":"real","kind":"depend","label":"controls"}],"shownClassIds":["subj","real"],"shownRelIds":["r1"],"activeIds":["real"]},"vars":[["RealImage","loads 5 MB on create"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":6,"narration":"ImageProxy implements the SAME interface and holds the real image. To a client it's just an Image, they can't tell the stand-in from the real thing.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["subj","real","proxy"],"shownRelIds":["r1","r2","r3"],"activeIds":["proxy"]},"vars":[["proxy","is-a Image, holds the real one"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":8,"narration":"Because the proxy sits on the same interface, it can intercept EVERY call and decide what to do before, or instead of, forwarding to the real subject.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["subj","real","proxy"],"shownRelIds":["r1","r2","r3"],"activeIds":["proxy","real"]},"vars":[["proxy","controls access"]]}]},{"label":"Lazy loading in action","code":["public void display() {","    if (real == null)","        real = new RealImage(file);   // expensive load, deferred","    real.display();                   // forward","}"],"steps":[{"view":"sequence","codeLine":2,"narration":"First display(): the proxy checks and sees the real image isn't loaded yet. So it CREATES it now, the expensive 5 MB load happens lazily, only when actually needed.","sequence":{"actors":[{"id":"c","label":"Client","kind":"actor"},{"id":"p","label":"ImageProxy","tint":"accent2"},{"id":"r","label":"RealImage"}],"messages":[{"id":"m1","from":"c","to":"p","label":"display()  (1st time)","kind":"call"},{"id":"m2","from":"p","to":"r","label":"load 5MB","kind":"create"},{"id":"m3","from":"p","to":"r","label":"display()","kind":"call"},{"id":"m4","from":"c","to":"p","label":"display()  (2nd time)","kind":"call"},{"id":"m5","from":"p","to":"r","label":"display()  (already loaded)","kind":"call"}],"shownCount":2,"activeIndex":1},"vars":[["1st call","loads then shows"]]},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":4,"narration":"With the real image now in hand, the proxy forwards display() to it. The client got its result; it never knew a load just happened.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":3,"activeIndex":2}},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":1,"narration":"Second display(): the real image already exists, so the proxy SKIPS the load and just forwards, access controlled, work deferred and done only once.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":5,"activeIndex":4},"vars":[["2nd call","reuses, just shows ✓"]]}]}]}}]]}]
